Silt REPL (type :quit to exit, :help for commands)
type Option(a) { Some(a), None }
type Result(a, e) { Ok(a), Err(e) }
type List(a)  -- builtin
Functions for working with ordered, immutable lists (`List(a)`).
type Map(a, b)  -- builtin
Functions for working with immutable, ordered maps (`Map(k, v)`).
type Int  -- builtin
Functions for parsing, converting, and comparing integers.
type Bool  -- builtin
type Bytes  -- opaque
trait Equal { fn equal(self, other: Self) -> Bool }
Whether two values are equal: `==` and `!=` need it.
trait Display { fn display(self) -> String }
How a value is shown: `println`, `print`, interpolation and `string.from` show it so.
trait Compare: Equal { fn compare(self, other: Self) -> Int }
The order of values: `<`, `>`, `<=` and `>=` need it.
trait Hash { fn hash(self) -> Int }
A value as a map's key or a set's element.
trait Error: Display { fn message(self) -> String }
An error a program reports: `message` says what went wrong.
trait Number {}
The types arithmetic is on, `Int` and `Float`: `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `%` and unary `-` need it.
type Option(a) { Some(a), None }
Constructs a present variant of `Option`.
type Option(a) { Some(a), None }
The absent variant of `Option`.
type Result(a, e) { Ok(a), Err(e) }
Constructs a success variant of `Result`.
type Result(a, e) { Ok(a), Err(e) }
Constructs an error variant of `Result`.
type Value { Null, Bool(Bool), Int(Int), Float(Float), String(String), Array(List(Value)), Object(Map(String, Value)) }
A JSON document as it is, for input whose shape is not known in advance: any document reads into it.
trait Encode { fn encode(self) -> Value }
What `json.stringify` and `json.pretty` need of the value they write.
trait Decode { fn decode(value: Value) -> Result(Self, JsonError) }
What `json.parse`, `json.parse_list`, `json.parse_map` and `json.decode` need of the type they decode into.
type ChannelOp(a) { Recv(Channel(a)), Send(Channel(a), a) }
Builds a receive arm for `channel.select`.
type ChannelOp(a) { Recv(Channel(a)), Send(Channel(a), a) }
Builds a send arm for `channel.select`.
type Selected(a) { Received(Channel(a), Option(a)), Sent(Channel(a)) }
What `channel.select` gives when an arm built with `channel.Send(ch, value)` completes: the value was handed off.
type Selected(a) { Received(Channel(a), Option(a)), Sent(Channel(a)) }
What `channel.select` gives when an arm built with `channel.Recv(ch)` completes: `channel.Received(ch, Some(value))` for a value, `channel.Received(ch, None)` when `ch` is closed and empty.
type ChannelResult(a) { Message(a), Empty, Closed }
Indicates the channel has been closed and is empty.
type ChannelResult(a) { Message(a), Empty, Closed }
Indicates the channel buffer is currently empty but not closed.
type ChannelResult(a) { Message(a), Empty, Closed }
Wraps a value received from a channel.
type Step(a) { Stop(a), Continue(a) }
Signals early termination from `list.fold_until`.
type Step(a) { Stop(a), Continue(a) }
Signals continuation in `list.fold_until`.
type IoError { NotFound(String), PermissionDenied(String), AlreadyExists(String), InvalidInput(String), Interrupted, UnexpectedEof, WriteZero, Other(String) }
type IoError { NotFound(String), PermissionDenied(String), AlreadyExists(String), InvalidInput(String), Interrupted, UnexpectedEof, WriteZero, Other(String) }
file or directory missing
type Handle(a)  -- opaque
type Weekday { Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday }
